WEBVTT

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.120
Exciting news, people!

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:40.332
The pet license
I requisitioned for Nibbler has arrived.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.125
Hermes, that's sweet.

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:43.961
I didn't know you cared about Nibbler.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.045
Dream on, woman.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.964
I'd like to put
the little bastard in a sack

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.967
and toss the sack in a river
and hurl the river into space.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.094
But I do like filling out requisitions,

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:53.637
and these were some doozies.

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:58.350
Great Jah's dreadlocks!
There's been a mix-up.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:01.270
This isn't a pet license,
it's a fishing license!

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:04.022
And it's mandatory!

00:01:16.802 --> 00:01:20.347
Ah. The exact center
of the Atlantic Ocean.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.183
This seems the logical place
for fish to congregate.

00:01:23.266 --> 00:01:25.352
So, we're in international waters?

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:26.812
Indeed so.

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:30.023
Falcon, this is Blue Raven.
The goose has nested.

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:32.109
Repeat, the goose has nested.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.824
Hey, guess what you're accessories to?

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:42.244
The sun, the sea air, good friends...

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:44.204
Leela's right. Fishing blows.

00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:45.789
What about making it interesting?

00:01:45.956 --> 00:01:47.457
- Why not?
- Yeah, cool.

00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:49.710
Everybody kick in five bucks.

00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:53.672
- There, wasn't that interesting?
- Bender!

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.717
This contest is as good as over.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.177
I once caught a fish this big.

00:01:59.261 --> 00:02:00.262
Oh, yeah?

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:02.639
I once caught a fish this big.

00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:06.101
I'm afraid you're
both out of your league, boys

00:02:06.184 --> 00:02:09.688
'cause you're looking at a woman
who owns her own harpoon.

00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:11.940
Harpoon, my ass.

00:02:12.024 --> 00:02:13.942
Okay.

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:18.363
Let's see now. Which bait to use?

00:02:18.447 --> 00:02:21.241
Crickets, squid, chicken necks?

00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:23.744
Excuse me. If I might be so bold,

00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:27.914
I'm willing to offer
my services as a bait critic.

00:02:27.998 --> 00:02:31.543
These sardines, for example,
are bland and tasteless.

00:02:33.587 --> 00:02:36.590
And these dry, stringy night crawlers,

00:02:36.673 --> 00:02:40.469
though juicy...
Very, very juicy...

00:02:44.056 --> 00:02:47.017
I don't believe this!
It's eating my bait!

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.769
Beat it, you mooching crawdad!

00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:57.611
Hey, Fry, check out
my laser-guided fishing rod.

00:02:57.694 --> 00:02:59.905
Quiet, Bender,
you're scaring away the fish.

00:02:59.988 --> 00:03:02.616
Fine. I'll head over
to the other side.

00:03:02.699 --> 00:03:05.410
Good luck fishing on this side!

00:03:09.498 --> 00:03:12.334
I can hit a fish between the eyes
from 20 yards.

00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:14.086
Oh, yeah? I can hit a shrimp.

00:03:14.169 --> 00:03:15.212
A shrimp?

00:03:15.237 --> 00:03:17.197
I find it a bit hard
to believe that...

00:03:19.257 --> 00:03:20.300
Ah-ha!

00:03:21.677 --> 00:03:23.178
Gather 'round, chumps.

00:03:23.261 --> 00:03:24.721
I got the winner!

00:03:26.473 --> 00:03:27.474
Aw.

00:03:27.557 --> 00:03:31.311
Oh, so this is where
you shop for your boots.

00:03:32.521 --> 00:03:35.524
Couple more of those
and you'll have yourself a fish stick.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.901
Hey!

00:03:37.985 --> 00:03:40.654
A fish this fine belongs
in a fish-nugget-style chunklet.

00:03:40.737 --> 00:03:43.156
Anyway, it's bigger
than anything you've caught.

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:48.896
Ow! My small intestine!

00:03:50.522 --> 00:03:51.815
Bingo!

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:55.527
Whatever it is,
it's 20 times heavier than a boot.

00:03:57.821 --> 00:03:58.947
Oh.

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:02.409
You'll never catch anything
with that primitive technology.

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:05.120
What you need is this fish pheromone,

00:04:05.204 --> 00:04:08.582
the most potent aphrodisiac
known to fishkind.

00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:12.544
Uh-oh.

00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:19.134
I'm so into you.

00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:23.805
Oh, my!

00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:26.517
Hey, Bender!

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.644
I just caught a fish this big.

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:30.437
Quit exaggerating, Fry.

00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:32.731
Ah, screw this.

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.858
If I'm not going to catch a fish,

00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:37.569
I might as well not catch a big fish.

00:04:38.487 --> 00:04:40.781
There. Like most of life's problems

00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:42.866
this one can be solved with bending.

00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:46.787
Bender, be careful!

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.373
That's the ship's diamond filament tether.

00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:50.457
It's unbreakable.

00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:52.209
Then why do I have to be careful?

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:55.087
It belonged to my grandmother.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.467
My manwich!

00:05:14.481 --> 00:05:15.732
Wake up, everyone!

00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:18.318
I've got something,
and this time it's alive.

00:05:21.238 --> 00:05:22.364
Oh!

00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:25.325
Dr. Zoidberg,
since when do you even wear boots?

00:05:25.409 --> 00:05:26.910
I wasn't wearing it.

00:05:26.994 --> 00:05:28.829
I was eating it.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.916
Come on, let's go home.

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:35.627
Sunburn!

00:05:35.711 --> 00:05:38.463
My fabulous body! It's ruined!

00:05:38.547 --> 00:05:40.424
What happened to my parasol?

00:05:40.507 --> 00:05:43.010
I don't know.
It wasn't here when I took your umbrella.

00:05:43.427 --> 00:05:45.971
What? I put sunblock on you.

00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:47.806
Well, it didn't work.

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:51.685
Come on, Bender.

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:53.896
Pull in your line, and let's go.

00:05:58.483 --> 00:06:00.235
Hey, I'm snagged.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.529
It's not snagged.

00:06:02.613 --> 00:06:04.990
The mechano-man has caught something.

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:13.582
Sweet zombie Jesus! It's huge!

00:06:13.665 --> 00:06:14.833
It's coming up!

00:06:22.049 --> 00:06:25.719
- Whoa, that's big!
- A colossal mouth bass!

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.098
It's diving!

00:06:31.808 --> 00:06:34.311
It's pulling us under!
Everyone, into the ship!

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:36.063
Wait, I'll save us.

00:06:36.146 --> 00:06:38.899
By cutting the unbreakable
diamond filament.

00:06:40.859 --> 00:06:43.695
Well, at least I'll die with my friends.

00:06:43.779 --> 00:06:44.780
Hello?

00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:55.999
My speedos!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.133
Depth at 45 hundred feet...

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:08.053
48 hundred, 50 hundred...

00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:09.763
5,000 feet.

00:07:09.847 --> 00:07:10.931
Dear lord!

00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:14.017
That's over 150 atmospheres of pressure!

00:07:14.101 --> 00:07:16.186
How many atmospheres
can the ship withstand?

00:07:16.311 --> 00:07:17.688
Well, it's a spaceship.

00:07:17.771 --> 00:07:20.315
So I'd say anywhere between zero and one.

00:07:22.526 --> 00:07:25.237
What's that? Is someone bending girders?

00:07:32.411 --> 00:07:34.621
We'll be crushed
if we don't equalize the pressure.

00:07:34.705 --> 00:07:35.831
How do we do that?

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:38.458
That should do it.

00:07:38.542 --> 00:07:40.127
We're all going to die!

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.004
Wait, I'll be back in a minute.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.017
- You did it, Fry!
- Did what?

00:08:02.065 --> 00:08:05.986
People, it's far, far worse
than we thought.

00:08:06.445 --> 00:08:08.280
My fish got away.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:14.161
There! good as new.

00:08:14.244 --> 00:08:16.205
Except that we're
three miles below the surface

00:08:16.288 --> 00:08:19.124
We don't have any food,
and the ship won't work underwater.

00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:20.834
Tempers are wearing thin.

00:08:20.918 --> 00:08:23.962
Let's just hope some robot
doesn't kill everybody.

00:08:24.046 --> 00:08:26.256
The important thing
is that we don't panic.

00:08:26.381 --> 00:08:29.051
There are rules for these situations.

00:08:29.134 --> 00:08:31.803
Now, the first order of business is lunch.

00:08:31.887 --> 00:08:33.889
I suggest a nice lobster Zoidberg.

00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:35.891
I mean, uh, lobster newburg.

00:08:35.974 --> 00:08:37.893
I mean, Dr. Zoidberg.

00:08:37.976 --> 00:08:40.062
Okay, everyone. Calm down.

00:08:40.145 --> 00:08:42.606
The professor and I
will get to work on the ship.

00:08:42.689 --> 00:08:45.400
Bender, Zoidberg,
since you can survive underwater,

00:08:45.484 --> 00:08:47.110
you'll go out and look for food.

00:08:47.194 --> 00:08:48.362
I better go, too.

00:08:48.445 --> 00:08:49.780
They don't know what I like.

00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:51.281
Fry, the pressure will crush you

00:08:51.406 --> 00:08:53.575
like a green snake
under a sugarcane truck!

00:08:53.659 --> 00:08:54.993
Not necessarily.

00:08:55.077 --> 00:08:57.329
This is a chance for Fry to test out

00:08:57.412 --> 00:08:59.748
my experimental anti-pressure pill.

00:09:00.499 --> 00:09:01.834
I can't swallow that.

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:03.627
Well, then, good news!

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:05.462
It's a suppository.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:11.510
How are you doing there, Fry?

00:09:15.013 --> 00:09:16.890
Glad to hear it.

00:09:17.474 --> 00:09:18.934
Ah!

00:09:22.271 --> 00:09:25.107
Oh, yeah!

00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:29.444
Yum, yum, yum.

00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.531
Uh-oh.

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:38.954
Look at me.

00:09:39.037 --> 00:09:42.457
I'm Dr. Zoidberg, homeowner.

00:09:47.254 --> 00:09:48.297
Careful, Fry.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.465
I think that flag might be poisonous.

00:09:50.549 --> 00:09:52.050
Ahoy, mateys!

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:54.178
I shanghaied us some hearty grub.

00:10:00.309 --> 00:10:03.353
The laws of science be a harsh mistress.

00:10:03.437 --> 00:10:06.940
Say, robot, old buddy,
could you help me move a couch?

00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:10.569
Uh... Okay,
but I'm not carrying it upstairs.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.883
What is it, Fry?

00:10:26.927 --> 00:10:29.638
You want some lemonade?
You saw a big parade?

00:10:29.721 --> 00:10:31.723
Your students loans have been repaid?

00:10:31.807 --> 00:10:34.184
Then how about lending
your old pal Zoidberg

00:10:34.268 --> 00:10:36.603
a few bucks, Mr. Millionaire?

00:10:41.692 --> 00:10:44.570
Fry, swallow your food, then talk.

00:10:46.029 --> 00:10:47.114
A mermaid!

00:10:47.236 --> 00:10:49.614
You think you saw a mermaid?

00:10:49.658 --> 00:10:52.411
No. I did see a mermaid.
She was wearing a tube top.

00:10:52.494 --> 00:10:54.538
And she had a beautiful, scaly tail

00:10:54.621 --> 00:10:56.540
and I think she had hair extensions.

00:10:56.623 --> 00:10:58.250
Yeah, right.

00:10:58.333 --> 00:11:01.712
You're simply hallucinating, you moron.

00:11:01.795 --> 00:11:03.922
What's so far-fetched about mermaids?

00:11:04.006 --> 00:11:06.133
There's all sorts of weird sea creatures

00:11:06.216 --> 00:11:08.343
here in the future, like Dr. Zoidberg.

00:11:11.279 --> 00:11:14.016
I'm afraid Fry is
suffering from ocean madness.

00:11:14.099 --> 00:11:16.226
Every time something good happens to me

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.812
you say it's some kind of madness
or I'm drunk

00:11:18.896 --> 00:11:20.314
or I ate too much candy.

00:11:20.397 --> 00:11:22.190
Well, I saw a real mermaid,

00:11:22.274 --> 00:11:25.777
and I wish my friends would have
the decency and kindness to believe me.

00:11:25.861 --> 00:11:27.905
Ocean madness.

00:11:29.823 --> 00:11:31.450
He may have ocean madness,

00:11:31.533 --> 00:11:34.202
but that's no excuse for ocean rudeness.

00:11:41.168 --> 00:11:43.337
"Ocean madness." Yeah, right.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.589
Yeah, it's always something, ain't it?

00:11:47.215 --> 00:11:48.258
It's her!

00:11:48.342 --> 00:11:50.177
Bender, wake up! She's here! wake up!

00:11:55.766 --> 00:11:57.601
Oh, oxygen.

00:12:06.693 --> 00:12:08.195
Here you go, darling.

00:12:09.404 --> 00:12:13.158
Hey, I can breathe.
And talk. Just like a fish.

00:12:13.242 --> 00:12:14.701
Oh, you speak fish?

00:12:16.787 --> 00:12:17.788
What?

00:12:17.871 --> 00:12:20.165
I'm sorry, my accent's atrocious.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.418
- Hi. My name's Umbriel.
- I'm Fry.

00:12:23.543 --> 00:12:25.963
So, uh, am I going to drown?

00:12:26.046 --> 00:12:27.673
'Course not. Just stay calm,

00:12:27.756 --> 00:12:30.342
and let the gentle currents
relax your every muscle.

00:12:32.575 --> 00:12:33.576
Oh, yeah!

00:12:33.613 --> 00:12:35.013
Did it just get warmer?

00:12:35.097 --> 00:12:37.140
I can't believe you're really real.

00:12:37.224 --> 00:12:38.267
I like your tail.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.643
Oh, you're sweet.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.565
I like those wiggly doodads
coming out of your hips.

00:12:42.604 --> 00:12:44.523
Thanks. They're called pants.

00:12:45.774 --> 00:12:47.484
This here's a volcanic vent.

00:12:47.568 --> 00:12:50.237
The water comes out at over 4,000 degrees.

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:51.405
No kidding?

00:12:53.115 --> 00:12:55.117
Did it just get colder?

00:12:56.827 --> 00:13:00.497
Tell me more about that bizarre
landy world you come from.

00:13:00.581 --> 00:13:02.165
Is there water there, too?

00:13:02.249 --> 00:13:04.501
Sure. Sometimes it falls from the sky.

00:13:04.585 --> 00:13:06.837
- Hmm.
- And sometimes it doesn't.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:10.716
Oh, Mr. Fry, you do go on.

00:13:10.799 --> 00:13:12.843
You know what I like
best about you, Umbriel?

00:13:12.926 --> 00:13:14.511
You find me fascinating

00:13:14.595 --> 00:13:17.514
Even when I'm not claiming to be
a jewel thief or a lion tamer.

00:13:17.598 --> 00:13:20.434
Lions? There are sea lions on the land?

00:13:20.517 --> 00:13:22.895
Yup. We call them "land sea lions."

00:13:22.978 --> 00:13:24.104
I tame them.

00:13:24.605 --> 00:13:29.693
Way down below the ocean

00:13:32.029 --> 00:13:37.451
Where I wanna be she may be

00:13:38.035 --> 00:13:42.497
Way down below the ocean

00:13:44.875 --> 00:13:50.380
Where I wanna be she may be

00:13:52.341 --> 00:13:56.220
I'm almost done reconfiguring
the ship's propulsion system.

00:13:56.303 --> 00:13:59.640
We can leave as soon as
the papier-mâche is dry.

00:13:59.723 --> 00:14:02.434
- Where's Fry?
- I didn't kill him. Professor?

00:14:02.517 --> 00:14:04.394
No, I've been busy.

00:14:04.478 --> 00:14:07.314
He must have gone out
looking for that "mermaid."

00:14:07.397 --> 00:14:09.316
The poor, demented honky.

00:14:09.399 --> 00:14:11.443
It's ocean madness, all right.

00:14:11.526 --> 00:14:15.239
Sailors call it "aqua dementia,"
"the deep down crazies,"

00:14:15.322 --> 00:14:17.991
"the wet willies,"
"the screaming moist..."

00:14:18.075 --> 00:14:19.826
We'll form a search party.

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.411
Now, we'll need oxygen.

00:14:21.495 --> 00:14:23.538
I got it covered.

00:14:23.622 --> 00:14:25.123
In the event of an emergency

00:14:25.207 --> 00:14:27.542
my ass can be used as a flotation device.

00:14:27.626 --> 00:14:28.752
Oh, that reminds me.

00:14:28.835 --> 00:14:31.088
You've all taken your
pressure pills, right?

00:14:31.171 --> 00:14:33.298
Yes. Stop asking.

00:14:39.012 --> 00:14:40.305
I've got his scent.

00:14:40.389 --> 00:14:42.683
Over here where the water gets warmer.

00:14:44.184 --> 00:14:45.477
This way.

00:14:52.693 --> 00:14:54.528
Bend me!

00:14:56.655 --> 00:14:57.656
Dude!

00:14:57.739 --> 00:14:59.533
An ancient sunken city!

00:15:01.952 --> 00:15:05.622
Could it possibly be?
Are the old legends true?

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:10.669
It is!

00:15:10.752 --> 00:15:14.631
It's the fabled Lost City of Atlanta!

00:15:14.715 --> 00:15:16.300
Howdy, y'all!

00:15:19.386 --> 00:15:21.013
Welcome to Atlanta.

00:15:21.096 --> 00:15:23.140
Folks 'round these parts
call me the Colonel.

00:15:26.351 --> 00:15:28.061
Here, have some breathers,

00:15:28.145 --> 00:15:30.230
courtesy of our Chamber of Commerce.

00:15:33.567 --> 00:15:36.612
This is uncomfortable and humiliating.

00:15:36.695 --> 00:15:39.740
Now, if they could put it
in the form of a suppository...

00:15:39.823 --> 00:15:41.283
Y'all enjoy your stay.

00:15:41.366 --> 00:15:43.827
Tourism's our main source
of income 'round here,

00:15:43.911 --> 00:15:46.330
so see the sights, spend some money...

00:15:46.413 --> 00:15:47.497
Please don't leave.

00:15:48.874 --> 00:15:49.875
Fry!

00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:52.127
Oh, I just knew you were still alive!

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:53.337
I owe you ten bucks, Hermes.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.006
Hey, you guys, the most
amazing thing happened.

00:15:56.089 --> 00:15:58.216
It's two-for-one Tuesday at Krispy Kreme.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:15:59.593
Plus, there's mermaids.

00:15:59.676 --> 00:16:00.844
Nice out-of-town folks,

00:16:00.928 --> 00:16:03.305
I'd like you to meet my daughter, Umbriel.

00:16:03.388 --> 00:16:05.724
Umbriel, these are some Yankees.

00:16:07.059 --> 00:16:08.143
So, Fry

00:16:08.227 --> 00:16:10.687
Atlanta was an American city in your time?

00:16:10.771 --> 00:16:12.397
I think it was just an airport.

00:16:12.481 --> 00:16:14.107
They had a place selling nuts.

00:16:14.191 --> 00:16:17.819
No! Ancient Atlanta was
more than just a Delta hub.

00:16:17.903 --> 00:16:22.157
It was a vibrant metropolis,
the equal of Paris or New York.

00:16:22.241 --> 00:16:24.368
That's right, honey. Whatever you say.

00:16:24.451 --> 00:16:26.578
Look at these fabulous ruins.

00:16:27.037 --> 00:16:30.374
Turner Field, the Coca-Cola Bottling Plant

00:16:30.499 --> 00:16:32.542
The, uh... The airport.

00:16:33.126 --> 00:16:37.047
But, tell us, how could a city
with such a fabulous airport

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.382
end up underwater?

00:16:38.465 --> 00:16:39.883
Ah, now, that's a story

00:16:39.967 --> 00:16:42.886
that can only rightly be told
in a Chamber of Commerce video

00:16:43.011 --> 00:16:45.722
narrated by folk-rock troubadour, Donovan.

00:16:48.976 --> 00:16:51.728
Atlanta was a city, landlocked,

00:16:51.812 --> 00:16:55.983
hundreds of miles from the area
we now call the Atlantic Ocean.

00:16:56.066 --> 00:16:59.444
Yet, so desperate the city's
desire for tourism

00:16:59.528 --> 00:17:02.072
that they moved offshore,
becoming an island

00:17:02.155 --> 00:17:04.575
and an even bigger Delta hub,

00:17:04.658 --> 00:17:07.995
until the city overdeveloped
and it started to sink.

00:17:09.454 --> 00:17:12.165
Knowing their fate,
the quality people ran away.

00:17:12.916 --> 00:17:16.378
Ted Turner, Hank Aaron, Jeff Foxworthy,

00:17:16.461 --> 00:17:20.048
the guy who invented Coca-Cola,
the magician,

00:17:20.132 --> 00:17:23.510
and the other so-called gods
of our legends...

00:17:23.594 --> 00:17:25.470
Though gods they were...

00:17:25.554 --> 00:17:27.556
And also, Jane Fonda was there.

00:17:28.223 --> 00:17:31.226
The others chose to remain
behind on their porches

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:35.856
with their rifles, and one day
evolve into mermaids

00:17:35.939 --> 00:17:39.484
and sing, and dance,and ring in the new.

00:17:39.568 --> 00:17:40.903
Hail Atlanta!

00:17:41.904 --> 00:17:43.947
- "The magician"?
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:17:44.031 --> 00:17:47.284
Wouldn't it take millions of years
to evolve into mermaids?

00:17:47.367 --> 00:17:48.785
Normally, yes.

00:17:48.869 --> 00:17:51.371
But the caffeine really sped things up.

00:17:51.496 --> 00:17:53.665
That stuff's wonderful.

00:17:54.666 --> 00:17:57.628
So, when Umbriel
first brought home this carpetbagger,

00:17:57.753 --> 00:17:58.837
I was agin' it.

00:17:58.921 --> 00:18:01.673
But damn if ol' legs here
ain't grown on me!

00:18:01.757 --> 00:18:03.425
Oh, shucks, Colonel.

00:18:05.469 --> 00:18:08.347
Well, it's all very nice here,
but we should be going.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.015
I miss me wife and me oxygen.

00:18:10.098 --> 00:18:12.935
Yes, we all miss our loved ones and gases.

00:18:13.018 --> 00:18:14.686
- Come on, Fry.
- Wait.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.188
I'm not going with you.

00:18:17.522 --> 00:18:19.358
But, Fry, what about us?

00:18:19.441 --> 00:18:21.777
What about your life on the surface?

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.278
You don't belong down here.

00:18:23.362 --> 00:18:24.363
She's right.

00:18:24.488 --> 00:18:28.075
I mean, sure, they got the Braves,
but it's a third-rate symphony.

00:18:28.158 --> 00:18:31.078
Fry, you half-mad, half-insane maniac,

00:18:31.161 --> 00:18:32.537
be reasonable.

00:18:32.621 --> 00:18:35.165
Don't you realize that
if you stay at this depth

00:18:35.249 --> 00:18:37.876
your body will permanently adapt
to the pressure?

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.045
Realize it? I don't even understand it.

00:18:40.128 --> 00:18:43.507
It means you'll never be able
to return to the surface.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.175
I don't care. I'm staying.

00:18:45.259 --> 00:18:46.843
I've got everything I want right here.

00:18:47.636 --> 00:18:50.222
I'm bored! Let's go.

00:18:51.765 --> 00:18:55.185
You know, Fry,
I've got a little place just outside town.

00:18:55.269 --> 00:18:56.812
You could come visit, maybe?

00:18:58.522 --> 00:18:59.648
Sorry, Zoidberg.

00:18:59.731 --> 00:19:01.358
I'm trying to join the Country Club.

00:19:03.068 --> 00:19:04.069
Fry!

00:19:06.613 --> 00:19:08.156
I'll miss you!

00:19:09.616 --> 00:19:11.743
Y'all come back, now, you hear?

00:19:11.827 --> 00:19:13.870
Let's go, damn it! Let's go!

00:19:17.457 --> 00:19:19.960
Well, I guess
this is good-bye for me as well.

00:19:20.043 --> 00:19:21.044
- Whatever.
- Later.

00:19:21.128 --> 00:19:22.129
Bye.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.261
My home!

00:19:29.344 --> 00:19:30.929
It burned down!

00:19:33.473 --> 00:19:35.767
How did this happen?

00:19:35.851 --> 00:19:37.853
That's a very good question.

00:19:37.936 --> 00:19:40.647
So, that's where I left my cigar.

00:19:40.731 --> 00:19:43.358
That just raises further questions.

00:19:43.442 --> 00:19:46.361
You know, Umbriel, these last 24 hours

00:19:46.445 --> 00:19:48.614
have been the happiest days of my life.

00:19:48.697 --> 00:19:53.368
Oh, Fry, I want you to make
a mer-woman out of mer-me.

00:19:56.663 --> 00:20:00.375
Mercy! I do believe
I'm gettin' the vapors.

00:20:06.465 --> 00:20:07.716
What the hell is that?

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:10.135
Yeah, I'm a little confused, too.

00:20:10.219 --> 00:20:13.138
How do I...
You know, with the tail and all?

00:20:13.222 --> 00:20:15.015
I'm not your first, am I?

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:17.559
I mean, I lay my eggs, then I leave

00:20:17.643 --> 00:20:19.603
and you release your fertilizer.

00:20:22.814 --> 00:20:24.775
Why couldn't she be
the other kind of mermaid

00:20:24.858 --> 00:20:27.694
with the fish part on top,
and the lady part on the bottom?

00:20:29.029 --> 00:20:32.199
Now, who's going to escort
me to the debutante ball?

00:20:32.282 --> 00:20:35.535
Well, what about that rich,
young dugong from Macon?

00:20:37.329 --> 00:20:39.915
There. The engine modifications
are complete.

00:20:39.998 --> 00:20:41.291
Prepare for launch.

00:20:46.838 --> 00:20:50.133
Wait! wait for me! Don't leave me here!

00:21:05.315 --> 00:21:08.777
And so, in honor
of his record-breaking catch,

00:21:08.902 --> 00:21:14.032
I'm proud to award Bender
this check for $1,000.

00:21:18.328 --> 00:21:20.497
- It's you!
- Hey, buddy!

00:21:20.581 --> 00:21:21.665
My manwich!

00:21:21.748 --> 00:21:24.293
Fry, are you all right? What happened?

00:21:24.376 --> 00:21:25.502
What about Umbriel?

00:21:25.586 --> 00:21:29.172
Well, it turns out I loved her,
but I wasn't "in love" with her.

00:21:29.256 --> 00:21:30.882
Trouble in bed.

00:21:30.966 --> 00:21:33.260
Ah, it's great to have you back, buddy.

00:21:33.343 --> 00:21:34.511
Wait...

00:21:34.595 --> 00:21:36.096
This is no record.

00:21:36.179 --> 00:21:37.639
Give me back that check.

00:21:37.764 --> 00:21:39.850
I'm giving it to some giant orphans.

00:21:41.518 --> 00:21:43.103
Ow! Bender, you're hurting me!

00:21:43.186 --> 00:21:45.689
Ow!

00:21:46.899 --> 00:21:49.902
Hey! I'm trying to sleep in here.

00:21:50.736 --> 00:21:52.654
Hail Atlanta.